---
description: When remediating Cognium SAST findings, verify sanitizers with MCP and keep fixes defensive.
globs: "**/*.{java,js,jsx,ts,tsx,mjs,cjs,py,go,rs,sh,bash,html,htm}"
alwaysApply: false
---

cognium-remediation: When writing or reviewing application code that may handle untrusted input, prefer engine-backed guidance from the `cognium` MCP server.

- Call `explain_finding` before rewriting a flagged sink.
- Call `check_sanitizer` before claiming a function sanitizes a given `sink_type`.
- Prefer cataloged sanitizers and safe APIs (parameterized queries, framework encoding, allowlisted path handling).
- After a fix, `refresh` and re-`scan` the same project root to confirm the finding is resolved.
- Do not add exploit samples, payloads, or attack procedures in comments, tests, or review notes.
